# consumers.txt - repos that VENDOR the engineering pack (skills/engineering/).
#
# A vendored file is a COPY. There is no live link back to this repo, so a fix here reaches a
# consumer only when someone re-runs `./setup.sh --vendor <path>` there. This file is that list: a
# repo missing from it does not get fixes, which is the exact failure mode the file prevents.
#
# Add a row the first time you vendor into a repo. Keep it to one line per consumer:
#
#     <path-or-slug>    <one-line note: what the repo is, anything the pack must know about it>
#
# Blank lines and lines beginning with `#` are ignored. Nothing parses this file today; it is for
# the human (or agent) doing a propagation sweep. Propagation flow: edit upstream, commit, re-run
# --vendor in each consumer, commit there, restart Claude Code if an agent changed. See
# skills/engineering/README.md.

# This file is the TEMPLATE. Copy it to `consumers.txt` (gitignored) and add your own rows:
#
#     cp consumers.txt.example consumers.txt
#
# The real list stays out of git deliberately: it names private repos and local paths, and it is
# operational to one machine rather than useful to a reader of the pack.

# <path-or-slug>    <what the repo is; anything the pack must know about it>
